{
  "mathematical_review": {
    "definitions": [
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 2472,
        "end_line": 15,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 2326,
        "start_line": 15,
        "text": "| `logic` | Are propositions, guards, quantifiers and inference rules explicit? | Missing evidence and cyclic self-support must not yield truth |\n",
        "text_sha256": "5488ae4d6b6749e14b4a2159b37c6e9a36f3bd443c25ca1241ad3f50e9383683"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 2665,
        "end_line": 16,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 2472,
        "start_line": 16,
        "text": "| `set_theory` | Are objects, membership, domains, products and cardinality bounds defined? | Test empty/duplicate inventories and distinguish finite sets from potentially unbounded families |\n",
        "text_sha256": "9f84ccff7910756b80b971f5a53048ac124b7c24bf9eb893beef0947b14f155c"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 2840,
        "end_line": 17,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 2665,
        "start_line": 17,
        "text": "| `type_theory` | Do constructors, domain/codomain and composition preserve declared types? | Reject a byte offset passed as a physical qubit ID or a mismatched composition |\n",
        "text_sha256": "1b3842a422fd7823abb0964d4a497e4a0e29a20333708d62a20c5d713449059a"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 3002,
        "end_line": 18,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 2840,
        "start_line": 18,
        "text": "| `arithmetic` | Are valuation, width, signedness, rounding and overflow specified? | Carry injection, XOR and assignment must produce distinct expected traces |\n",
        "text_sha256": "e17214597016152cb07a7034f4d0f74bedfc90bcaf26492c7a0588ac40aa34b2"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 3187,
        "end_line": 19,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 3002,
        "start_line": 19,
        "text": "| `algebra` | Which laws actually hold: closure, associativity, identity, inverse, distributivity? | Noninvertible masks cannot be admitted as group elements under the same operation |\n",
        "text_sha256": "92e1103169ba86a0cee341f08439bef17ba84f222f217361208efdf66f0bec8c"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 3380,
        "end_line": 20,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 3187,
        "start_line": 20,
        "text": "| `order_lattices` | Is the relation a partial/total order; are meets/joins defined where claimed? | Test antisymmetry/transitivity and incomparable cases rather than infer order from labels |\n",
        "text_sha256": "1e9a2ae90a05832916ce98c6fe1c4b1d40e3125c4e257b0c0fc51bf3d999821c"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 3547,
        "end_line": 21,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 3380,
        "start_line": 21,
        "text": "| `combinatorics` | What is counted and what is the finite search bound? | Candidate programs, distinct functions and successful outputs have different denominators |\n",
        "text_sha256": "5d34154fba1a3f504ee0fb8d11ecc2338dacf16ceaf192ac6ab07af8acd71e25"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 3699,
        "end_line": 22,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 3547,
        "start_line": 22,
        "text": "| `graph_theory` | What do vertices/edges, direction and weights mean? | Different edge types and disconnected components must remain distinguishable |\n",
        "text_sha256": "865481924f65a78f40a6569d18b4ebc240b02fd3e11dd9e6867d9330e661a20f"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 3871,
        "end_line": 23,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 3699,
        "start_line": 23,
        "text": "| `automata_languages` | What grammar, states, transitions, guards and acceptance rules execute? | Test rejected words, illegal transitions, cycles and budget exhaustion |\n",
        "text_sha256": "d70bd0aca4f6fba21a9a8fe91fd81debbca01427435e16b503d12a00113b4ff5"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 4064,
        "end_line": 24,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 3871,
        "start_line": 24,
        "text": "| `information_coding` | What information is preserved, compressed or lost under the codec? | Retain source bytes; test tampering, alternate encoding, distribution shift and noninvertibility |\n",
        "text_sha256": "6ca78c8a7eb5bf3c0652badb6c424ac049b8e32e7df0e2b56baa21ebfb6db5e6"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 4221,
        "end_line": 25,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 4064,
        "start_line": 25,
        "text": "| `geometry` | What coordinate spaces, units, metrics and transformations are admitted? | Move layout origins without changing a function or quantum state |\n",
        "text_sha256": "1d87a6ac844596888351d99b0786752ea80830e9112f8a8e3938ae4bdba6b4d8"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 4387,
        "end_line": 26,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 4221,
        "start_line": 26,
        "text": "| `topology` | What cover/complex/topology and continuity conditions support the claim? | A graph one-skeleton and a filled complex need not have the same homology |\n",
        "text_sha256": "f7be689afa9b178be885b528e2736d827f6e0341a1a2335e20b8dc4c27fc0e6e"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 4563,
        "end_line": 27,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 4387,
        "start_line": 27,
        "text": "| `analysis_calculus` | What domains, regularity, derivatives, measures and convergence conditions apply? | Test boundaries, nondifferentiable cases and sampling ambiguities |\n",
        "text_sha256": "293a32b1243a862a5fd66ddf3b5e822a274cb6e5801456bbb0f34ea1aa308296"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 4745,
        "end_line": 28,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 4563,
        "start_line": 28,
        "text": "| `differential_equations` | What evolution law, initial/boundary data and well-posedness assumptions apply? | Compare analytic solutions and convergence under a refined time step |\n",
        "text_sha256": "c34b102ec458e0ff720c4806406264e386ccd71572719f41ff8801bce2c010a6"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 4934,
        "end_line": 29,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 4745,
        "start_line": 29,
        "text": "| `spectral_harmonic` | What basis, transform normalization, window and spectral interpretation apply? | Test phase loss, aliasing, Parseval conventions and failed inverse reconstruction |\n",
        "text_sha256": "cf73110e08c15a210a80c4e4517f092069f4b15a262499e4e512164c2794ce4b"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 5158,
        "end_line": 30,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 4934,
        "start_line": 30,
        "text": "| `probability_statistics` | What random process, likelihood, estimator, independence and uncertainty are assumed? | Null controls, held-out data, multiple-testing corrections and equal probabilities with different states |\n",
        "text_sha256": "9eac27cae07c1eeb9a3fae80fb606053a47f0ab9bad7a2318907a05d3d26c316"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 5363,
        "end_line": 31,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 5158,
        "start_line": 31,
        "text": "| `optimization_control` | What objective, constraints, admissible controls and termination criteria are used? | Compare a strong baseline; distinguish a local/search-order optimum from a global optimum |\n",
        "text_sha256": "4f0472b849a6c49f471fe8ce93f9d2e9d7af6df42fdb9cb748615c1ca1815491"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 5556,
        "end_line": 32,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 5363,
        "start_line": 32,
        "text": "| `numerical_analysis` | What precision, conditioning, stability and error/tolerance contract applies? | Cross-implementation comparison, malformed/nonfinite input and changed discretization |\n",
        "text_sha256": "d635d5a42186e8775bee261f95e500cd5a533ec746a41316a4a38f0b9ec61bc4"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 5750,
        "end_line": 33,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 5556,
        "start_line": 33,
        "text": "| `category_composition` | What objects/morphisms compose; do identity, associativity and preservation diagrams hold? | Type-compatible syntax alone does not prove a functor or naturality law |\n",
        "text_sha256": "c861f491d38d7eb2a0ad033102028eb9ec868db04635e9beeebe2dbfd6951372"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 5955,
        "end_line": 34,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 5750,
        "start_line": 34,
        "text": "| `physics_units` | What physical model, dimensional analysis, conserved quantities and regime apply? | Do not infer force/energy from layout distance or equate dark-current calibration with dark matter |\n",
        "text_sha256": "4f779f1e11d9331ce7ede9826e5f3334f9530a000f0d802a18a781ffd22aa31b"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 6162,
        "end_line": 35,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 5955,
        "start_line": 35,
        "text": "| `quantum_information` | What state/channel/measurement semantics, basis order and equivalence convention apply? | Relative-phase, positivity, CPTP, measurement-loss and logical/physical-address controls |\n",
        "text_sha256": "4ec2bb79ee0563f8284aa041a3db78b4a405a2bae02422128240e34f211d93ce"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 6345,
        "end_line": 36,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 6162,
        "start_line": 36,
        "text": "| `computation_complexity` | What are state/search/work/memory bounds and the cost model? | Distinguish logical fuel, gate count, serialized bytes, elapsed time and resident memory |\n",
        "text_sha256": "4f4a54ba4ac21072869ea0aa86f97e1cde0067f755de559d19f4feb040c9400b"
      },
      {
        "end_byte_exclusive": 6546,
        "end_line": 37,
        "source": {
          "bytes": 41427,
          "path": "docs/MATHEMATICAL_ATLAS.md",
          "sha256": "529dbf8e2977129ae4203604d9ed91eb9ae6319a50cfc380e50ea64d6ce27ca6"
        },
        "start_byte": 6345,
        "start_line": 37,
        "text": "| `metrology_uncertainty` | What was measured, with which calibration, traceability and error propagation? | Distinguish simulated output from observation and stale calibration from current evidence |\n",
        "text_sha256": "ee9a6c0e135858909d8d86597ccefd65384d467037a70e190752a645db953752"
      }
